/*
Problem: Largest Number (LC 179)
Topic: Greedy / Custom Sorting

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Convert every integer into a string.

Sort the strings so that, for any two
strings a and b:

a comes before b if

a + b > b + a

This ordering guarantees that the
final concatenated number is as large
as possible.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Convert all integers to strings.

2. Sort using the comparator:

   a + b > b + a

3. Concatenate all sorted strings.

4. If the first character is '0',
   return "0" because all numbers are
   zeros.

5. Otherwise, return the result.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

[10,2]

Compare:

"210" > "102"

So,

2 comes before 10.

Answer:

"210"

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

[3,30,34,5,9]

Sorted order:

9

5

34

3

30

Concatenation:

9534330

Answer:

"9534330"

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

For any two numbers, placing them in
the order that produces the larger
concatenation always contributes to
the globally largest number.

The custom comparator enforces this
ordering throughout the sort.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n log n × k)

n = number of elements

k = average number of digits

Sorting dominates the complexity.

Space : O(n × k)

Strings are stored separately.

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Greedy + Custom Comparator Sorting
*/

class Solution {
public:

    static bool cmp(string a, string b) {

        // Choose the better ordering
        return a + b > b + a;
    }

    string largestNumber(vector<int>& nums) {

        vector<string> v;

        // Convert integers to strings
        for (int num : nums) {
            v.push_back(to_string(num));
        }

        // Sort using custom comparator
        sort(v.begin(), v.end(), cmp);

        string ans = "";

        // Build final number
        for (string& s : v) {
            ans += s;
        }

        // Handle all-zero case
        if (ans[0] == '0')
            return "0";

        return ans;
    }
};
